[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug, one fix queued. The reports merged into it hold three problems,
and the queued parser fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket. Shipping the parser fix will not stop the others.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems

1. **Shared parser reads day-first dates month first** —
   [ticket #1](https://github.com/kbuksakowski/mega-dev-support-desk/issues/1). The `parser` row above,
   counted the way the desk files reports: by tenant, the one-day moves in its footnote included. Every tenant on file writes the day first; the parser reads
   month first, so day and month swap.
2. **booking-v3 form hints MM/DD/YYYY but reads the date day first** —
   [ticket #2](https://github.com/kbuksakowski/mega-dev-support-desk/issues/2). The `hint` row above, the
   one marked as having no ticket of its own. People type what the hint tells them; the form reads it the
   tenant's way. A different code path: the parser fix will not close it.
3. **Invite date moves by one day** —
   [ticket #4](https://github.com/kbuksakowski/mega-dev-support-desk/issues/4). The reports in the footnote
   under the table (`desk-notes.json`). Day and month do not swap; the date lands one day off, or differs by
   where the client is.

## Why it looked like one bug

- **Merged by subject.** [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line
  alone. "Wrong date" reads the same whatever caused it, so three problems landed in one ticket.
- **Intake tags are a guess.** Intake tags a report `hint` when the reporter's browser is `en-US` and
  `parser` otherwise. The browser is not the tenant, so the "tagged as" column disagrees with the cause.
  Count by the tenant's locale and booking form, not by tag.
- **The desk saw the one-day moves** after #4471 was marked known and noted them, but only as a footnote,
  with no ticket of their own.

## What to change

- Keep #4471 for the parser. Move the form-hint and one-day reports to their tickets.
- Merge by cause, not by subject. Decision 0001 needs a new record; it is not edited.
- Before a big ticket is marked known, split it by cause and count once per problem.

